import GroupApproximation.Manuscript.ChainCore.BilateralThreeCellDischarge
import GroupApproximation.Meta.AxiomGuard

/-!
# nm-chain-15: `EL_3(S)` for the special ring `S = cellRing` (carto re-audit)

`non_mf_groups_exist.tex`, proof of `prop:bilateral-three` (tex 1554–1557):

> The unital subalgebra $S\subseteq pR_Xp$ generated by $s=up$, $t=pu^{-1}$ and $kp$
> satisfies $ts=p$, $st=p-d$.  It is finitely generated, so $L=\EL_3(S)$ has
> property~\textup{(T)}.  Embed it in $\GL_3(R_X)$ by adjoining identity on $1-p$.

## Audit (carto re-audit OK)

* **Generators.** `cellRing T k hP hTP` (`ChainCore/BilateralThreeCellDischarge.lean:64`) is
  the subring of the corner `pR_Xp` generated by the finite set
  `{sCorner, tCorner} ∪ {p (a·1) p | a ∈ k}`, i.e. `s = up`, `t = pu⁻¹` and `kp`, as printed.
  It is finitely generated (`isFinitelyGeneratedRing_cellRing`, line 69).
* **Embedding.** `Cell.cornerEmbed` (`Algebra/BilateralThreeCellCorner.lean:120`) sends `g`
  to `diag(1-p) + g`, "adjoining identity on `1-p`"; it is injective
  (`cornerEmbed_injective`) and its range is `coreGroup` of the coefficients of `S`
  (`range_cornerEmbed`).
* **(T).** `hasKazhdanPropertyT_range_of_injective`
  (`ChainCore/BilateralThreeCorollaries.lean:53`) transports EJZ at `n = 3` along the
  injective embedding.

The theorem below is `hasKazhdanPropertyT_bilateralCoreGroup`
(`ChainCore/BilateralThreeZSentences.lean:97`) with the abbreviation `bilateralCellSet`
unfolded, stated over the built discharge module only, so this lane does not depend on the
nm-chain-11 module `BilateralThreeZSentences`.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation.Manuscript.NonMF.ChainCarto15

/-- **"$L=\EL_3(S)$ has property (T)"** (tex 1556), for `L` the image of `EL_3(cellRing)` in
`GL_3(R_X)` under the corner embedding. -/
theorem hasKazhdanPropertyT_bilateralCoreGroup' {X : Type} [TopologicalSpace X]
    (T : X ≃ₜ X) (k : Type) [Field k] [Finite k] {P : Set X} (hP : IsClopen P)
    (hTP : T '' P ⊆ P) :
    GroupApproximation.HasKazhdanPropertyT.{0, 0}
      ↥(GroupApproximation.BilateralThreeCell.coreGroup
        (Set.range fun a :
            ↥(GroupApproximation.Manuscript.ChainCore.BilateralThree.cellRing T k hP hTP) =>
          (a : (GroupApproximation.ClopenCrossedProduct.bilateralCell T k hP hTP).Corner).1)) := by
  rw [← (GroupApproximation.ClopenCrossedProduct.bilateralCell T k hP hTP).range_cornerEmbed
    (GroupApproximation.Manuscript.ChainCore.BilateralThree.cellRing T k hP hTP)]
  exact GroupApproximation.Manuscript.ChainCore.BilateralThree.hasKazhdanPropertyT_range_of_injective
    (GroupApproximation.Manuscript.ChainCore.BilateralThree.isFinitelyGeneratedRing_cellRing
      T k hP hTP) _
    ((GroupApproximation.ClopenCrossedProduct.bilateralCell T k hP hTP).cornerEmbed_injective _)

#audit_axioms hasKazhdanPropertyT_bilateralCoreGroup'

end GroupApproximation.Manuscript.NonMF.ChainCarto15
